/-!
# Critical-path nonnormality and factorization setup

This interface exports the three factorization clauses of source 2.2.  Clause
(iv) gives the actual subgroup containment and relative nonnormality, clause
(v) uses the literal universal escape premise and backward path extension, and
clause (vi) constructs offenders for both endpoint layers with their actual
quotient conjugation actions and fixed-subgroup identifications.

Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher (1993), pp.856--857.
-/
